<title>USA: U.S., Florida orange crop estimates--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S., Florida orange crop estimates--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA orange production estimates (crop in 1,000 boxes, yield in gallons/box at 42.0 degrees Brix basis):</p>
<p>    -			1996/97:	Indicated</p>
<p>    -		 April 1  Prev.Est.  1995/96</p>
<p> Florida Oranges  221,200   220,000   203,200</p>
<p> Florida Temples    2,500     2,500     2,150</p>
<p> Fla. FCOJ Yield     1.57	1.54	1.52</p>
<p> U.S. Oranges     294,920   289,850   271,790</p>
<p>Note-U.S. oranges and Florida oranges exclude temples.  </p>
<p>Florida orange production estimate was increased from a record 220.0 million boxes estimated in March.</p>
<p>Market analysts had expected the box count to remain flat at 222 million 90-lb boxes, and predicted the Florida frozen concentrated orange juice yield would rise slightly from 1.54 gallons per box.</p>
</text>
